            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis and biological evaluation of novel 6,11-dihydro-5H-benzo[e]pyrimido- [5,4-b][1,4]diazepine derivatives as potential c-Met inhibitors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>212-228</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0223-5234(17)30672-4</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ejmech.2017.08.060</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Over expression of c-Met tyrosine kinase is known to promote tumorigenesis and metastasis, as well as to cause therapeutic resistance. Herein a series of novel 6,11-dihydro-5H-benzo[e]pyrimido[5,4-b][1,4]diazepine derivatives were designed, synthesised and evaluated for their c-Met kinase inhibition. Compounds 17e, 17f, 18a, and 18b were further examined for their anti-proliferative activities against four typical cancer cell lines (PC-3, Panc-1, HepG2, and Caki-1). The promising compound 17f was identified as a multi-target receptor tyrosine kinase inhibitor, which also displayed favourable pharmacokinetic properties in rats, had an acceptable safety profile in preclinical studies, and significant anti-tumour activity in the Caki-1 tumour xenograft model.</AbstractText>
